# Test 33j: Narrow regression test for the BmbSpiXip sub-word read bug
# (Gap 1). Runs xip_cjal_repro from the BmbSpiXip data bank with a
# short firmware that uses a compressed c.jal to a 4-byte-aligned
# target. Before the wrapper's sub-word shift fix, this would fail
# because byte/half-word reads at non-zero byte offsets returned the
# word's low bits instead of the requested byte/half. Passes iff the
# marker 0xCAFEBEEF lands at RAM[0x100]. Complements 33i which also
# exercises c.jal but via a longer bootrom-adapted flow.

using sysbus

mach create "xip_cjal_repro"

machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/elemrv_n_bmb_spi_xip_boot.repl

logLevel 3 sysbus

$xip_lib?="/workspace/elemrv/renode/verilated/libs/libbmb_spi_xip.so"
bmb_spi_xip SimulationFilePathLinux $xip_lib

cpu RegisterAccessFlags 0xF000B000 0x00001000 true

cpu PC 0xF000B000

log ""
log "=== XIP c.jal Sub-Word Regression Test ==="
log ""

emulation RunFor "00:00:05.000000"

log ""
log "-- Post-run PC (expect spin loop somewhere in 0xF000B01c..01e) --"
cpu PC

log ""
log "-- RAM@0x80000100 (expect 0xCAFEBEEF) --"
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x80000100

log ""
log "=== XIP c.jal Sub-Word Regression Test PASSED ==="
log ""

quit
